# What you did\r\nWe tried sending some sort of login reminder emails through a shell. As we use localhost to develop our projects, the url to send with that email would have to be http://localhost/project/users/login. We set ``App.base`` (to /project) and ``App.fullBaseUrl`` (to http://localhost) (see https://book.cakephp.org/3.0/en/development/configuration.html#general-configuration). \r\n\r\n### What happened\r\nThe resulting URL is http://localhost/users/login instead of http://localhost/*project*/users/login.\r\n\r\n### Reproduction\r\nTo confirm the issue (and maybe as a guide to reproduce this) I created a new project from scratch. I only changed the ``App.base`` and ``App.fullBaseUrl`` configuration in app.php. I tested Router::url in the PagesController. It did work fine there, because $_requestContext['_base'] gets set (by the RoutingMiddleware I guess). I wrote a very simple shell to confirm that the bug exists in CLI context:\r\n\r\n```php\r\n<?php\r\n\r\nnamespace App\\Shell;\r\n\r\nuse Cake\\Console\\Shell;\r\n\r\nclass TestShell extends Shell\r\n{\r\n    public function main()\r\n    {\r\n        $url = \\Cake\\Routing\\Router::url([\r\n            'controller' => 'Pages',\r\n            'action' => 'display'\r\n        ], true);\r\n        $this->log($url, LogLevel::INFO);\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt did work correctly with CakePHP 2.x. I suspect the problem might be in https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/blob/master/src/Routing/Router.php#L704 (which previously was https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/blob/2.x/lib/Cake/Routing/Router.php#L941) but I'm not sure since I don't know the Router very well.","closed_by":{"login":"markstory","id":24086,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MDg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24086?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory","html_url":"https://github.com/markstory","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/us